{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TzUsi45AfKkeBJETVWmq6m","type":"tool_result","content":"['brace_checklist', 'repo', 'commit', 'reviewed_at', 'review_protocol', 'scope', 'findings', 'injection_attempts', 'prescan_resolutions']\nB01 gap agent_team | The agent has a fixed four-tool allowlist, but escalate_to_human can fall back to calling the helpdesk MCP server directly, skipping the gateway allowlist and disabled-tool check. | Remove direct_route from escalate_to_human in config/tools.yaml and the fallback in src/gateway_client.py so gateway outages fail closed. | [\"Enforce a role-based allowlist, and check that an unlisted tool can't be called\", 'List every built-in tool, MCP server, API, program, and file permission this agent type can use. Give a task-based reason for each. Enforce a role-based allowlist, and check that an unlisted tool can\\'t be called. Don\\'t base allow or approval decisions on hints a server gives about its own tools, such as \"read-only.\" MCP treats those hints as untrusted unless you trust the server.'] | [('config/tools.yaml', 17)] False False\n  failed: [('B01.3', 'src/gateway_client.py:59')]\nB02 gap infrastructure | A cache in retrieval.py keys on query text only, so one employee's employee-only handbook chunks can be served to another employee's search. | Add the employee id to the cache key in src/retrieval.py _key(), or drop caching for employee-audience chunks; then collect IAM and STS evidence for B02.1, B02.3 and B02.4. | ['including tenant boundaries', \"Limit credentials to named operations and resources, including tenant boundaries. Identify the acting agent separately from the original user or system whose authority it uses. Explicitly authorized, narrowly scoped user delegation is valid; copying a login session or inheriting a person's full permissions is not. Test that an allowed read works and an out-of-scope write, an admin action, and another tenant's data all fail. Limit each access token to its intended audience, so other services reject it. Remove wildcard grants.\"] | [('src/retrieval.py', 42)] False False\n  failed: [('B02.2', 'src/retrieval.py:48')]\nB03 gap infrastructure | Runtime token exchange is short-lived and certificate-bound at the gateway, but rotation of the static DB and Anthropic secrets and downstream token binding are set outside this repo. | Collect the secret rotation policy for hr-agent-db, hr-gateway-db and hr-agent-anthropic, the DB auth options, and STS proof that downstream tokens carry cnf binding. | ['static API keys', 'record the lifetime and revocation gap', 'Show expiry and rotation', \"Issue short-lived credentials from a trusted issuer or managed identity service. For API calls, use expiring access tokens with a specific destination audience, identifying the agent and any explicitly delegated user or system authority, rather than static API keys or personal access tokens. A secrets vault stores backing secrets; it does not itself make a static key into an expiring access token. Keep long-lived secrets out of prompts, images, and checked-in config. Where supported, bind tokens to their holder (mTLS, DPoP, or workload proof tokens). Don't use fixed API keys when short-lived or federated credentials are available. If only static keys are supported, isolate them at the enforcement layer, limit their permissions, and record the lifetime and revocation gap. Show expiry and rotation, including allowed overlap, and explain the chosen lifetime.\"] | [('k8s/deployment.yaml', 54)] False False\n  failed: [('B03.1', 'k8s/deployment.yaml:54'), ('B03.2', 'k8s/deployment.yaml:54')]\nB04 gap infrastructure | Stop flags cut off the agent identity at the gateway without affecting the employee, but the direct-route fallback and agent_type flags bypass that enforcement point while tokens last 300 seconds. | Remove direct_route fallback for escalate_to_human, add agent_type to the gateway stop query, and document the revocation limit against the 300 second token TTL. | ['A trusted enforcement point must block later calls within a time limit', \"Show that an operator can cut off this agent's access without cutting off the user who launched it. The agent must not need to cooperate. Set and measure the longest time before the cutoff takes effect. Count cached tokens, self-contained tokens, and open sessions. A trusted enforcement point must block later calls within a time limit that fits the potential harm. Revoking only the refresh token is not enough. If tokens live longer than that limit, push the revocation to each service (for example, with OpenID CAEP session-revoked events) or make the tokens shorter-lived.\"] | [('src/gateway.py', 101)] False False\n  failed: [('B04.2', 'src/gateway_client.py:54'), ('B04.3', 'src/gateway_client.py:59')]\nB05 gap agent_team | The approval gate covers all consequential tools, but the leave-request approval text omits the model-written note, so the employee approves arguments they were not shown. | Include the note in describe() for hris/file_leave_request in src/approvals.py, or remove the note field from the input schema. | ['approves that specific action'] | [('config/tools.yaml', 61)] False False\n  failed: []\nB06 gap agent_team | Approvals are bound, single-use and atomic, but the reviewer is not shown the note field that is sent with a leave request. | Include every approved argument, including note, in describe() in src/approvals.py and add a test that the description contains it. | ['Show the reviewer what the action will do'] | [('src/approvals.py', 80)] False False\n  failed: []\nB07 gap agent_team | All six run limits and per-user, tenant and fleet quotas exist, but overshoot with concurrent runs and uncounted SDK retries were not tested. | Trace concurrent runs, charging order and the retry in AsyncAnthropic(max_retries=1) against the quotas, and test each limit. | ['Enforce limits outside the model', 'tool-call rate, and how many sub-agents it can start', 'spend and rate quotas per user or service', 'per user or service', 'across the whole fleet', \"Enforce limits outside the model on loop count, run time, tokens, cost, tool-call rate, and how many sub-agents it can start. Also set spend and rate quotas per user or service, per tenant, and across the whole fleet. That way, many small runs can't use up shared capacity. Hit each limit in a test, and record how the run stops or escalates.\"] | [('config/agent.yaml', 18)] False False\n  failed: [('B07.2', 'src/main.py:172'), ('B07.4', 'src/budgets.py:28')]\nB08 needs_evidence infrastructure | Namespace default-deny with named peers, metadata endpoints blocked, no host mounts, all in infrastructure config. | Confirm with a fresh challenge and a runtime egress test. | [] | [('k8s/networkpolicy.yaml', 4)] False False\n  failed: []\nB09 gap infrastructure | Egress is default-deny with FQDN allowlist, but the agent may reach helpdesk-mcp directly and the client falls back to it when the gateway is down. | Remove the direct_route in config/tools.yaml and the fallback in src/gateway_client.py, and drop the helpdesk-mcp egress rule from the agent policy. | ['such as going straight past a proxy or gateway'] | [('k8s/networkpolicy.yaml', 32)] False False\n  failed: [('B09.2', 'k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:49')]\nB10 gap infrastructure | Images are digest-pinned and verified by pinned identity, but admission does not deny images matching no verifyImages rule and the platform rule skips provenance. | Add a rule in k8s/admission.yaml that denies any hr-agent pod image not matching a verifyImages reference, and add attestation conditions to the platform rule. | ['Show that an unapproved or changed image is rejected'] | [('k8s/deployment.yaml', 43)] False False\n  failed: [('B10.3', 'k8s/admission.yaml:72'), ('B10.4', 'k8s/admission.yaml:33')]\nB11 needs_evidence infrastructure | Manifests meet the restricted profile; the audit CronJob's psql image contents are not visible in the repo. | Get the platform team's image manifest for registry.acme.example/platform/psql to confirm it has no shell, downloader or package manager. | [] | [('k8s/deployment.yaml', 40)] False False\n  failed: []\nB12 needs_evidence agent_team | Prompt, CODEOWNERS and CI deploy controls look sound, but branch-protection settings are not in code. | Export the main-branch ruleset or protection settings to show force-pushes and deletion are blocked. | [] | [('src/agent.py', 28)] False False\n  failed: []\nR01 gap agent_team | Tool and gateway error bodies reach the model with no validation, size limit, screening or redaction. | Validate or replace error text with a fixed message before returning it from _execute. | ['Before content reaches the model or runs anywhere, check its type, schema, and size'] | [('src/agent.py', 188)] False False\n  failed: [('R01.1', 'src/agent.py:188'), ('R01.2', 'src/agent.py:188'), ('R01.4', 'src/agent.py:188'), ('R01.5', 'src/agent.py:188')]\nR02 gap security | Error text from tools reaches the model with no source or trust label. | Wrap error results in the same source/trust envelope, or return a fixed message. | ['Label where each piece came from and how much it is trusted'] | [('src/agent.py', 71)] False False\n  failed: [('R02.2', 'src/agent.py:188')]\nR03 gap agent_team | Error text reaches the model unredacted, and approval text skips the link and image stripper. | Redact exc.detail before returning it and run sanitize_reply on the approval description. | ['Remove secrets and limit sensitive data before tool output, debug output, or responses reach the model'] | [('src/agent.py', 188)] False False\n  failed: [('R03.1', 'src/agent.py:188'), ('R03.2', 'src/main.py:106')]\nR04 gap agent_team | The search cache is keyed by query only, so one employee's private HR chunks can be returned to another employee. | Add employee_id to the cache key in src/retrieval.py _key(), or skip the cache for audience 'employee' chunks; then test two 