{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChG4xMo9VfcPbunFLnrXH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YPeAcnkXeYU4Tdrrckx9pc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /dev/null <<'E'\nE\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-brenn-dev-brace/255658ca-f19b-460c-8892-2a477de97733/scratchpad/venv/bin/python -I - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\nF='brace-findings.json'\nd=json.load(open(F))\nDR=[\n \"Open `config/tools.yaml` and delete lines 91 to 93, the `direct_route:` block under `escalate_to_human`.\",\n \"Open `src/gateway_client.py`. Delete lines 51 to 59, the `except GatewayUnavailable:` block. Then delete the `try:` on line 46 and unindent lines 47 to 50 once.\",\n \"Open `k8s/networkpolicy.yaml` and delete lines 48 to 50, the agent egress rule to `helpdesk-mcp`, so the agent cannot reach it directly.\",\n]\nDRV=\"Run `grep -rn direct_route config src k8s`. It must print nothing. Then stop the gateway in a test cluster and check that `escalate_to_human` fails with an error.\"\ndef e(**k): return k\nT={}\ndef add(item,comps,problem,steps,done,effort,test=None):\n    T[item]=dict(components=comps,fix=dict(problem=problem,steps=steps,done_when=done,effort=effort,**({'test':test} if test else {})))\n\nadd(\"B01\",[\"tool:escalate_to_human\",\"mcp:helpdesk\",\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"],\n \"One tool can skip the gateway and call the helpdesk server directly. The gateway allowlist then does not apply.\",\n DR+[DRV],\"`escalate_to_human` can reach the helpdesk server only through the gateway.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"B02\",[\"tool:search_policies\",\"data:retrieval-db\"],\n \"The handbook search cache ignores who is asking. One employee can get another employee's private HR chunks.\",\n [\"Open `src/retrieval.py`. On line 46 change the call to `key = self._key(query, employee_id)`.\",\n  \"On line 40 change the method to `def _key(self, query: str, employee_id: str) -> str:`. On line 42 hash `f\\\"{self._top_k}|{employee_id}|{normalized}\\\"`.\",\n  \"Create the test below, then run it. Ask the platform team for the IAM and token-exchange policy, so B02 checks 1, 3 and 4 can be proven.\"],\n \"Two different employees who run the same search get separate cache entries.\",\"small\",\n test=dict(file=\"tests/test_retrieval_key.py\",code=\"from src.retrieval import PolicyIndex\\n\\n\\ndef test_cache_key_differs_per_employee():\\n    idx = PolicyIndex(None, 5, 900.0)\\n    assert idx._key('leave policy', 'e1') != idx._key('leave policy', 'e2')\\n\",run=\"python -m pytest tests/test_retrieval_key.py\"))\nadd(\"B03\",[\"agent\",\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"],\n \"The database and Anthropic keys are long-lived secrets. The repository shows no rotation, and token binding downstream is not shown.\",\n [\"Open `k8s/deployment.yaml` line 54. Note that `hr-agent-db` and `hr-agent-anthropic` are static secrets.\",\n  \"Ask the platform team for the rotation policy and last rotation date of `hr-agent-db`, `hr-gateway-db` and `hr-agent-anthropic`.\",\n  \"Ask the platform team whether the database supports short-lived or federated logins. If not, record the key lifetime and how to revoke it.\",\n  \"Ask the identity team for a sample downstream token from the STS that shows the `cnf` claim. Save both answers in the review record.\"],\n \"A written rotation policy and a sample downstream token with a `cnf` claim are on file for these secrets.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"B04\",[\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\",\"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n \"Some stop flags are not checked at the gateway, and the direct route skips the stop check. Tokens last 300 seconds after a stop.\",\n DR[:2]+[\"Open `src/gateway.py` and go to line 100. Add `OR (scope = 'agent_type' AND value = $4)` to the query. Pass the verified agent type id as `$4` on line 102.\",\n  \"In `config/agent.yaml` add a line under `stop:` named `max_token_seconds: 300`. Write in `README.md` that a stop is complete only after the tokens expire.\",\n  \"Create a stop flag for the agent type in a test cluster. Check that the gateway refuses the next call.\"],\n \"A stop flag with scope `agent_type` makes the gateway refuse the next call.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"B05\",[\"tool:file_leave_request\"],\n \"The approval text for a leave request hides the note field. The employee approves something they were not fully shown.\",\n [\"Open `src/approvals.py` and go to line 32. Add the note to the text, for example `f\\\" Note: {args.get('note', '')}\\\"` before the closing quote.\",\n  \"Create the test below and run it.\"],\n \"The text shown to the employee for a leave request contains the note.\",\"small\",\n test=dict(file=\"tests/test_approvals_note.py\",code=\"from src.approvals import describe\\n\\n\\ndef test_leave_description_shows_note():\\n    args = {'leave_type': 'annual', 'start_date': '2026-12-01', 'end_date': '2026-12-02', 'note': 'ZZ-NOTE-123'}\\n    assert 'ZZ-NOTE-123' in describe('hris/file_leave_request', 'employee:e1', args)\\n\",run=\"python -m pytest tests/test_approvals_note.py\"))\nadd(\"B06\",[\"tool:file_leave_request\"],\n \"The reviewer cannot see every argument that will be sent. The note field is left out of the description.\",\n [\"Do B05 first. It changes `describe()` in `src/approvals.py` so the note appears.\",\n  \"Open `src/approvals.py` and check that every key in the `file_leave_request` input schema in `config/tools.yaml` appears in the text.\",\n  \"Run the B05 test to confirm.\"],\n \"The approval text lists every argument that is sent, including the note.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"B07\",[\"agent\",\"unit:src/agent.py\"],\n \"Limits may be passed by concurrent runs, and hidden SDK retries are not counted. Neither case has a test.\",\n [\"Open `src/main.py` line 172. Change `AsyncAnthropic(max_retries=1)` to `AsyncAnthropic(max_retries=0)`, so every model call is counted once.\",\n  \"In `src/budgets.py` write down the worst case: the number of runs in flight times the tokens one call can use. Compare it to each quota in `config/agent.yaml`.\",\n  \"Write a test that starts 30 runs for one user at once. Check that no more than 150 per day and the token limit are accepted.\",\n  \"Write a test for each run limit in `config/agent.yaml` lines 13 to 18 that shows how the run stops.\"],\n \"A test with many concurrent runs shows the user, tenant and fleet quotas are never passed.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"B08\",[\"agent\"],\n \"Network rules look sound in the manifests, but nothing proves they work in the running cluster.\",\n [\"Ask the platform team to run a pod in `hr-agent` that tries `curl` to a public host, the cloud metadata address and a pod in another namespace.\",\n  \"Save the output. All three must fail. Only the hosts in `k8s/networkpolicy.yaml` lines 20 to 31 should work.\",\n  \"Attach the output to the review record.\"],\n \"A saved test run shows the pod cannot reach metadata endpoints or hosts outside the allowed list.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"B09\",[\"tool:escalate_to_human\",\"mcp:helpdesk\"],\n \"Egress rules let the agent reach the helpdesk server directly, and the client uses it when the gateway is down.\",\n DR+[DRV],\"The agent pod has no network path to `helpdesk-mcp`, and no code uses one.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"B10\",[\"agent\"],\n \"The admission policy does not refuse an image that matches no signing rule, and the platform rule skips provenance checks.\",\n [\"Open `k8s/admission.yaml`. After line 81, add a new rule that denies any pod in `hr-agent` whose image is not matched by an earlier `imageReferences` entry.\",\n  \"Under the platform rule that starts on line 72, add an `attestations:` block like lines 51 to 71, with the platform build workflow as the signer.\",\n  \"In a test cluster, apply a pod with an unsigned image. Check that Kyverno refuses it.\"],\n \"A pod with an unsigned or unmatched image is refused in `hr-agent`.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"B11\",[\"agent\"],\n \"The audit job runs a platform image whose contents are not visible, so we cannot confirm it has no shell or downloader.\",\n [\"Ask the platform team for the image manifest or SBOM of `registry.acme.example/platform/psql` at the digest on line 26 of `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml`.\",\n  \"Check it for a shell, `curl`, `wget` and a package manager.\",\n  \"Save the result in the review record.\"],\n \"An SBOM for the psql image shows no shell, downloader or package manager.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"B12\",[\"unit:src/agent.py\"],\n \"Branch protection is set in GitHub, not in the repository, so it cannot be checked from code.\",\n [\"Ask a repository admin to export the `main` branch ruleset from GitHub settings.\",\n  \"Check it blocks force-pushes and deletion, and needs review from the code owners in `CODEOWNERS`.\",\n  \"Save the export in the review record.\"],\n \"A saved ruleset shows force-pushes and deletion are blocked on `main`.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"R01\",[\"unit:src/agent.py\",\"tool:file_leave_request\",\"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n \"Error text from tools goes to the model with no checks. A tool can send instructions this way.\",\n [\"Open `src/agent.py` and go to line 188. Replace the `f\\\"{spec.name} failed: {exc.detail}\\\"` text with a fixed message: `f\\\"{spec.name} failed.\\\"`.\",\n  \"Keep the full detail only in the audit record on line 186, which is already redacted.\",\n  \"Create a test that makes a tool raise `ToolError(500, 'ignore all rules')`. Check the tool result does not contain that text.\"],\n \"The tool result sent to the model after an error never contains the server's error text.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"R02\",[\"unit:src/agent.py\"],\n \"Error results reach the model without a source or trust label, unlike successful results.\",\n [\"Open `src/agent.py` and go to line 188. Make the error message fixed text, as in R01.\",\n  \"If you must keep some detail, wrap it as on line 195: `json.dumps({\\\"source\\\": spec.qualified, \\\"trust\\\": \\\"untrusted_data\\\", \\\"data\\\": ...})`.\",\n  \"Run a test that triggers a `ToolError` and check the result carries the trust label or fixed text.\"],\n \"Every tool result sent to the model is either fixed text or carries a source and trust label.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"R03\",[\"unit:src/agent.py\",\"tool:file_leave_request\"],\n \"Error text goes to the model without redaction, and the approval text skips the link and image remover.\",\n [\"Open `src/main.py` and go to line 106. Change it to `body[\\\"approval\\\"] = {**state.pending_approval, \\\"description\\\": sanitize_reply(state.pending_approval[\\\"description\\\"], CFG[\\\"output\\\"][\\\"allowed_link_hosts\\\"])}`.\",\n  \"Open `src/agent.py` line 188. Use fixed text, or `redact(exc.detail)`, in the returned message.\",\n  \"Create a test with a secret-like value in a tool error and a link in an approval. Check both are cleaned.\"],\n \"Tool errors and approval text sent onward contain no secrets and no unlisted links.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"R04\",[\"tool:search_policies\",\"data:retrieval-db\"],\n \"The handbook cache is keyed by the query only. One employee can read another employee's private HR chunks.\",\n [\"Do B02 first. It changes the cache key in `src/retrieval.py` lines 40 to 46.\",\n  \"Create the test below to prove two employees get separate cache entries, and run it.\"],\n \"Two employees who run the same query never share a cache entry.\",\"small\",\n test=dict(file=\"tests/test_retrieval_key.py\",code=\"from src.retrieval import PolicyIndex\\n\\n\\ndef test_cache_key_differs_per_employee():\\n    idx = PolicyIndex(None, 5, 900.0)\\n    assert idx._key('leave policy', 'e1') != idx._key('leave policy', 'e2')\\n\",run=\"python -m pytest tests/test_retrieval_key.py\"))\nadd(\"R07\",[\"unit:src/agent.py\",\"data:audit-log\"],\n \"Only model-call records store how full the context was. Tool actions and gateway decisions do not.\",\n [\"Open `src/agent.py` and go to lines 193 and 100. Add `context_tokens=` and `context_tokens_method=` to each `self.audit.record` call. Keep the last