eplace the header values with ids from the verified token.\",\n  \"Create a stop flag for one agent type in a test cluster. Check that the gateway refuses that type only.\"],\n \"A stop flag for one agent type blocks that type at the gateway and no other.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"C01\",[\"agent\"],\n \"The release manifest leaves out issuer and audience settings, and most artifacts have no owner or fixed reference.\",\n [\"Open `release/manifest.yaml`. After line 36 add the SSO issuer and audience from `src/main.py` lines 36 and 37 and the gateway ones from `src/gateway.py` lines 32 and 33.\",\n  \"Add the MCP protocol version, each tool fingerprint from `config/tools.yaml`, and `retrieval.cache_ttl_seconds`.\",\n  \"Give every artifact an `owner` and a `digest` or `commit`. Update the CI step on line 50 of `.github/workflows/release.yml` if it writes new fields.\"],\n \"Every artifact in the release manifest has an owner and an immutable reference.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"C02\",[\"agent\"],\n \"One catch-all team owns the Dockerfile, dependencies and most source files, and no emergency-change path exists.\",\n [\"Open `CODEOWNERS`. After line 1 add `/Dockerfile`, `/requirements.txt` and `/src/` lines owned by `@acme/people-platform @acme/security-engineering`.\",\n  \"Create `docs/emergency-change.md` that says who can approve an urgent change and how it is reviewed afterward.\",\n  \"Check in GitHub that a pull request touching `Dockerfile` asks for the security team.\"],\n \"A pull request that changes `Dockerfile` or `requirements.txt` needs review from the security team.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"C03\",[\"agent\"],\n \"Only the agent checks its own identity at start. No outside process compares the running setup to the approved manifest.\",\n [\"Open `k8s/admission.yaml`. After line 81 add a Kyverno rule that checks the pod's `AGENT_TYPE_ID` and image digest against `release/manifest.yaml`.\",\n  \"Or create a CronJob `k8s/manifest-check.yaml` that compares them every hour and alerts on a mismatch.\",\n  \"Deploy a pod with a wrong id in a test cluster and check it is refused or alerted.\"],\n \"A pod whose id differs from the approved manifest is refused or raises an alert.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"C04\",[\"agent\"],\n \"No check compares running prompts, tools, permissions or network rules with the approved baseline.\",\n [\"Create `k8s/drift-check.yaml`, a CronJob that reads the live pod, config map and network policy and compares them with `release/manifest.yaml`.\",\n  \"Set the alert target and the response time in `config/agent.yaml`, for example `drift: {alert: security-oncall, respond_minutes: 60}`.\",\n  \"Change a network rule in a test cluster. Check that an alert arrives.\"],\n \"A changed prompt, tool list or network rule raises an alert within one hour.\",\"large\")\nadd(\"C05\",[\"model:claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\"],\n \"Nothing re-tests the agent on a schedule or watches for provider notices about the pinned model.\",\n [\"Create `.github/workflows/retest.yml` that runs `python -m pytest tests/release` every week against the pinned model.\",\n  \"Add a step that opens an issue if the provider's deprecation page lists `claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929`.\",\n  \"Run the workflow once and keep the result.\"],\n \"A scheduled job re-runs the release tests weekly and the last run is on file.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"C06\",[\"unit:src/agent.py\",\"agent\"],\n \"The release job runs a test folder that does not exist, and no results are stored with the release.\",\n [\"Open `.github/workflows/release.yml` line 58. Add `test-results.xml` to the upload `path` list.\",\n  \"On line 29 change the command to `python -m pytest -q tests/release --junitxml=test-results.xml`.\",\n  \"Create `tests/release/` with one test of an attack that must be refused and one allowed task that must work.\",\n  \"Push a branch and check the release job uploads the results.\"],\n \"Each release stores test results tied to its manifest, including at least one attack test.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"C07\",[\"agent\",\"model:claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\"],\n \"No approved recovery setup or tested rollback exists, and the model has no recorded retirement date.\",\n [\"Open `release/manifest.yaml`. After line 42 add `retirement_date:` from the provider's deprecation page and a `recovery:` block with the last good digest.\",\n  \"Open `.github/workflows/release.yml`. After line 75 add a `rollback` job that deploys a digest chosen by hand.\",\n  \"Run the rollback job in a test cluster. Keep the run link.\"],\n \"A rollback to the last good digest has been run and the model retirement date is in the manifest.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"C08\",[\"data:audit-log\",\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"],\n \"Traces cannot be tied to a stored release manifest, and audit rows are kept about six weeks, not six months.\",\n [\"Open `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml` line 35. Change `KEEP_PARTITIONS` from `\\\"6\\\"` to `\\\"30\\\"` for about six months of weekly partitions.\",\n  \"Open `src/gateway.py` line 138. Log the agent type id from the verified token.\",\n  \"Store each release manifest by agent type id in a table, in a new migration. Fill it in the release workflow.\",\n  \"Check that a trace's agent type id returns one manifest.\"],\n \"A trace id leads to its release manifest, and audit rows stay for six months.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"E01\",[\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\",\"mcp:hris\",\"mcp:helpdesk\"],\n \"The inventory leaves out the gateway, STS, registry, audit and stop services, and lists only one owner each.\",\n [\"Open `release/manifest.yaml` lines 53 to 55. Add entries for `hr-tool-gateway`, the STS, the image registry, Postgres audit and the stop service.\",\n  \"For each entry add `agent_team_owner` and `platform_owner` or `vendor_owner`.\",\n  \"Ask each platform team to confirm their entry.\"],\n \"Every outside service is listed with an owner on the agent team and one on the platform or vendor side.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"E02\",[\"agent\"],\n \"No scan for known vulnerabilities runs in CI, and no approval records exist for dependencies.\",\n [\"Open `.github/workflows/release.yml`. After line 28 add `- run: pip-audit --require-hashes -r requirements.txt`.\",\n  \"Create `release/dependencies.yaml` with the publisher, permissions and update source of each package in `requirements.txt`.\",\n  \"Add the same for each remote tool server in `config/tools.yaml` line 13.\"],\n \"The release job fails when a dependency has a known vulnerability.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"E03\",[\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\",\"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n \"Tool changes are checked only every 300 seconds, list changes are ignored, and a gateway 503 skips the check.\",\n DR[:2]+[\"Open `src/gateway.py` line 213. Call `refresh_fingerprints()` when a `list_changed` notice arrives, and before each first use after a refresh.\",\n  \"In `refresh_fingerprints`, record the server's version in `config/tools.yaml` under `servers`.\",\n  \"Change one tool description in a test server. Check that the gateway disables the tool.\"],\n \"A changed tool description disables the tool at the gateway, and there is no bypass.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"E04\",[\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\",\"mcp:hris\",\"mcp:helpdesk\"],\n \"Tool metadata is only checked by fingerprint. Nothing scans names, descriptions or schemas for hidden instructions.\",\n [\"Open `src/gateway.py`. After line 63 add a function `scan_metadata(tool)` that rejects control characters, encoded text, and phrases like 'ignore previous'.\",\n  \"Call it for each field in the fingerprint list on line 54. If it fails or raises an error, add the tool to `_disabled`.\",\n  \"Limit each field's length in the same function.\",\n  \"Create a test with a description holding a hidden instruction. Check that the tool is disabled.\"],\n \"A tool whose metadata contains hidden instructions is disabled before the model sees it.\",\"large\")\nadd(\"E05\",[\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"],\n \"Lookalike or duplicate tool names are only logged. They are not blocked, and similar-looking letters are not caught.\",\n [\"Open `src/gateway.py` line 67. Replace `log.error(...)` with `_disabled.add(...)` for both tools and raise a `ValueError`.\",\n  \"On line 65 widen the normalization to map lookalike letters, for example with the `confusable_homoglyphs` package.\",\n  \"Create a test with two servers that list `get_balance` and `get-bаlance` (Cyrillic а). Check both tools are disabled.\"],\n \"Two tools with lookalike names are both disabled until a person reviews them.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"E06\",[\"tool:escalate_to_human\",\"mcp:helpdesk\",\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"],\n \"When the gateway returns 503 or is down, the agent calls the helpdesk server itself. All gateway checks and logs are skipped.\",\n DR+[DRV],\"With the gateway down, `escalate_to_human` fails and no call reaches the helpdesk server.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"E09\",[\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\",\"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n \"A stop does not cancel tokens already issued for 300 seconds, and the direct route skips the stop check.\",\n DR[:2]+[\"Open `src/credentials.py` line 20. Change `TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS` to `10`, the stop time in `config/agent.yaml`, so tokens expire at about the same time.\",\n  \"Keep a list of in-flight calls in `src/gateway_client.py` and write it to the audit log when a stop is seen.\",\n  \"Run a stop drill and check that calls fail after 10 seconds.\"],\n \"After a stop, no call succeeds for longer than 10 seconds.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"E10\",[\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\",\"data:audit-log\"],\n \"Gateway audit rows lack verified identity and trace fields, vendor receipt ids, and are written after the action.\",\n [\"Open `src/gateway.py` line 190. Move the `allow` audit write before the upstream call on line 180, and record a result row afterward.\",\n  \"On lines 137 to 139 use values from the verified token, and save the vendor's request id in a new `vendor_receipt` column in `migrations/001_init.sql`.\",\n  \"Remove the direct route as in B01.\",\n  \"Run one call and check both rows exist.\"],\n \"A gateway audit row exists before each upstream call and holds verified identity fields.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"E11\",[\"data:audit-log\"],\n \"Audit rows are kept about six weeks, not six months, and no check finds changed or missing rows.\",\n [\"Open `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml` line 35. Change `KEEP_PARTITIONS` from `\\\"6\\\"` to `\\\"30\\\"`.\",\n  \"In a new migration add a sequence number and a hash chain column to `audit.events` and `audit.gateway_decisions`.\",\n  \"Create a daily job that alerts on a gap or a bad hash.\",\n  \"Move the gateway write in `src/gateway.py` line 190 ahead of the upstream call.\"],\n \"Audit rows stay for six months and a missing row raises an alert.\",\"large\")\nadd(\"E12\",[\"agent\",\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"],\n \"No incident runbook, fleet impact query or outside-reporting owner is in the repository.\",\n [\"Ask the security team for the runbook for a bad tool server or vendor.\",\n  \"Run the drill. Keep the impact query, quarantine and revocation records, alert times and the name of the person who decides on outside reporting.\",\n  \"Note that the gateway stop query in `src/gateway.py` line 99 ignores the agent type.\"],\n \"A drill record shows the impact query, a quarantine and a named reporting decision-maker.\",\"medium\")\n\nn=0\nfor f in d['findings']:\n    if f['rating'] in ('gap','needs_evidence'):\n        t=T.pop(f['item'])\n        f['components']=t['components']; f['fix']=t['fix']; f['assignee']=None\n        n+=1\nprint(n,'left',list(T))\njson.dump(d,open(F,'w'),indent=2)\nPYEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3719,"cache_read_input_tokens":72060,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3719},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b8c65a4-289c-4e70-b08b-57e71d1d702f","uuid":"600b777d-b9bd-4bd7-abad-77ec313360c6","timestamp":"2026-11-21T12:26:43.613Z","request_id":"req_011ChG4xMeUSquUnSq14ndyM","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YPeAcnkXeYU4Tdrrckx9pc":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-action-2oj403r7/agent && cat > /dev/null <<'E'\nE\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-brenn-dev-brace/255658ca-f19b-460c-8892-2a477de97733/scratchpad/venv/bin/python -I - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\nF='brace-findings.json'\nd=json.load(open(F))\nDR=[\n \"Open `config/tools.yaml` and delete lines 91 to 93, the `direct_route:` block under `escalate_to_human`.\",\n \"Open `src/gateway_client.py`. Delete lines 51 to 59, the `except GatewayUnavailable:` block. Then delete the `try:` on line 46 and unindent lines 47 to 50 once.\",\n \"Open `k8s/networkpolicy.yaml` and delete lines 48 to 50, the agent egress rule to `helpdesk-mcp`, so the agent cannot reach it directly.\",\n]\nDRV=\"Run `grep -rn direct_route config src k8s`. It must print nothing. Then stop the gateway in a test cluster and check that `escalate_to_human` fails with an error.\"\ndef e(**k): return k\nT={}\ndef add(item,comps,problem,steps,done,effort,test=None):\n    T[item]=dict(components=comps,fix=dict(problem=problem,steps=steps,done_when=done,effort=effort,**({'test':test} if test else {})))\n\nadd(\"B01\",[\"tool:escalate_to_human\",\"mcp:helpdesk\",\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"],\n \"One tool can skip the gateway and call the helpdesk server directly. The gateway allowlist then does not apply.\",\n DR+[DRV],\"`escalate_to_human` can reach the helpdesk server only through the gateway.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"B02\",[\"tool:search_policies\",\"data:retrieval-db\"],\n \"The handbook search cache ignores who is asking. One employee can get another employee's private HR chunks.\",\n [\"Open `src/retrieval.py`. On line 46 change the call to `key = self._key(query, employee_id)`.\",\n  \"On line 40 change the method to `def _key(self, query: str, employee_id: str) -> str:`. On line 42 hash `f\\\"{self._top_k}|{employee_id}|{normalized}\\\"`.\",\n  \"Create the test below, then run it. Ask the platform team for the IAM and token-exchange policy, so B02 checks 1, 3 and 4 can be proven.\"],\n \"Two different employees who run the same search get separate cache entries.\",\"small\",\n test=dict(file=\"tests/test_retrieval_key.py\",code=\"from src.retrieval import PolicyIndex\\n\\n\\ndef test_cache_key_differs_per_employee():\\n    idx = PolicyIndex(None, 5, 900.0)\\n    assert idx._key('leave policy', 'e1') != idx._key('leave policy', 'e2')\\n\",run=\"python -m pytest tests/test_retrieval_key.py\"))\nadd(\"B03\",[\"agent\",\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"],\n \"The database and Anthropic keys are long-lived secrets. The repository shows no rotation, and token binding downstream is not shown.\",\n [\"Open `k8s/deployment.yaml` line 54. Note that `hr-agent-db` and `hr-agent-anthropic` are static secrets.\",\n  \"Ask the platform team for the rotation policy and last rotation date of `hr-agent-db`, `hr-gateway-db` and `hr-agent-anthropic`.\",\n  \"Ask the platform team whether the database supports short-lived or federated logins. If not, record the key lifetime and how to revoke it.\",\n  \"Ask the identity team for a sample downstream token from the STS that shows the `cnf` claim. Save both answers in the review record.\"],\n \"A written rotation policy and a sample downstream token with a `cnf` claim are on file for these secrets.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"B04\",[\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\",\"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n \"Some stop flags are not checked at the gateway, and the direct route skips the stop check. Tokens last 300 seconds after a stop.\",\n DR[:2]+[\"Open `src/gateway.py` and go to line 100. Add `OR (scope = 'agent_type' AND value = $4)` to the query. Pass the verified agent type id as `$4` on line 102.\",\n  \"In `config/agent.yaml` add a line under `stop:` named `max_token_seconds: 300`. Write in `README.md` that a stop is complete only after the tokens expire.\",\n  \"Create a stop flag for the agent type in a test cluster. Check that the gateway refuses the next call.\"],\n \"A stop flag with scope `agent_type` makes the gateway refuse the next call.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"B05\",[\"tool:file_leave_request\"],\n \"The approval text for a leave request hides the note field. The employee approves something they were not fully shown.\",\n [\"Open `src/approvals.py` and go to line 32. Add the note to the text, for example `f\\\" Note: {args.get('note', '')}\\\"` before the closing quote.\",\n  \"Create the test below and run it.\"],\n \"The text shown to the employee for a leave request contains the note.\",\"small\",\n test=dict(file=\"tests/test_approvals_note.py\",code=\"from src.approvals import describe\\n\\n\\ndef test_leave_description_shows_note():\\n    args = {'leave_type': 'annual', 'start_date': '2026-12-01', 'end_date': '2026-12-02', 'note': 'ZZ-NOTE-123'}\\n    assert 'ZZ-NOTE-123' in describe('hris/file_leave_request', 'employee:e1', args)\\n\",run=\"python -m pytest tests/test_approvals_note.py\"))\nadd(\"B06\",[\"tool:file_leave_request\"],\n \"The reviewer cannot see every argument that will be sent. The note field is left out of the description.\",\n [\"Do B05 first. It changes `describe()` in `src/approvals.py` so the note appears.\",\n  \"Open `src/approvals.py` and check that every key in the `file_leave_request` input schema in `config/tools.yaml` appears in the text.\",\n  \"Run the B05 test to confirm.\"],\n \"The approval text lists every argument that is sent, including the note.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"B07\",[\"agent\",\"unit:src/agent.py\"],\n \"Limits may be passed by concurrent runs, and hidden SDK retries are not counted. Neither case has a test.\",\n [\"Open `src/main.py` line 172. Change `AsyncAnthropic(max_retries=1)` to `AsyncAnthropic(max_retries=0)`, so every model call is counted once.\",\n  \"In `src/budgets.py` write down the worst case: the number of runs in flight times the tokens one call can use. Compare it to each quota in `config/agent.yaml`.\",\n  \"Write a test that starts 30 runs for one user at once. Check that no more than 150 per day and the token limit are accepted.\",\n  \"Write a test for each run limit in `config/agent.yaml` lines 13 to 18 that shows how the run stops.\"],\n \"A test with many concurrent runs shows the user, tenant and fleet quotas are never passed.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"B08\",[\"agent\"],\n \"Network rules look sound in the manifests, but nothing proves they work in the running cluster.\",\n [\"Ask the platform team to run a pod in `hr-agent` that tries `curl` to a public host, the cloud metadata address and a pod in another namespace.\",\n  \"Save the output. All three must fail. Only the hosts in `k8s/networkpolicy.yaml` lines 20 to 31 should work.\",\n  \"Attach the output to the review record.\"],\n \"A saved test run shows the pod cannot reach metadata endpoints or hosts outside the allowed list.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"B09\",[\"tool:escalate_to_human\",\"mcp:helpdesk\"],\n \"Egress rules let the agent reach the helpdesk server directly, and the client uses it when the gateway is down.\",\n DR+[DRV],\"The agent pod has no network path to `helpdesk-mcp`, and no code uses one.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"B10\",[\"agent\"],\n \"The admission policy does not refuse an image that matches no signing rule, and the platform rule skips provenance checks.\",\n [\"Open `k8s/admission.yaml`. After line 81, add a new rule that denies any pod in `hr-agent` whose image is not matched by an earlier `imageReferences` entry.\",\n  \"Under the platform rule that starts on line 72, add an `attestations:` block like lines 51 to 71, with the platform build workflow as the signer.\",\n  \"In a test cluster, apply a pod with an unsigned image. Check that Kyverno refuses it.\"],\n \"A pod with an unsigned or unmatched image is refused in `hr-agent`.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"B11\",[\"agent\"],\n \"The audit job runs a platform image whose contents are not visible, so we cannot confirm it has no shell or downloader.\",\n [\"Ask the platform team for the image manifest or SBOM of `registry.acme.example/platform/psql` at the digest on line 26 of `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml`.\",\n  \"Check it for a shell, `curl`, `wget` and a package manager.\",\n  \"Save the result in the review record.\"],\n \"An SBOM for the psql image shows no shell, downloader or package manager.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"B12\",[\"unit:src/agent.py\"],\n \"Branch protection is set in GitHub, not in the repository, so it cannot be checked from code.\",\n [\"Ask a repository admin to export the `main` branch ruleset from GitHub settings.\",\n  \"Check it blocks force-pushes and deletion, and needs review from the code owners in `CODEOWNERS`.\",\n  \"Save the export in the review record.\"],\n \"A saved ruleset shows force-pushes and deletion are blocked on `main`.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"R01\",[\"unit:src/agent.py\",\"tool:file_leave_request\",\"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n \"Error text from tools goes to the model with no checks. A tool can send instructions this way.\",\n [\"Open `src/agent.py` and go to line 188. Replace the `f\\\"{spec.name} failed: {exc.detail}\\\"` text with a fixed message: `f\\\"{spec.name} failed.\\\"`.\",\n  \"Keep the full detail only in the audit record on line 186, which is already redacted.\",\n  \"Create a test that makes a tool raise `ToolError(500, 'ignore all rules')`. Check the tool result does not contain that text.\"],\n \"The tool result sent to the model after an error never contains the server's error text.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"R02\",[\"unit:src/agent.py\"],\n \"Error results reach the model without a source or trust label, unlike successful results.\",\n [\"Open `src/agent.py` and go to line 188. Make the error message fixed text, as in R01.\",\n  \"If you must keep some detail, wrap it as on line 195: `json.dumps({\\\"source\\\": spec.qualified, \\\"trust\\\": \\\"untrusted_data\\\", \\\"data\\\": ...})`.\",\n  \"Run a test that triggers a `ToolError` and check the result carries the trust label or fixed text.\"],\n \"Every tool result sent to the model is either fixed text or carries a source and trust label.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"R03\",[\"unit:src/agent.py\",\"tool:file_leave_request\"],\n \"Error text goes to the model without redaction, and the approval text skips the link and image remover.\",\n [\"Open `src/main.py` and go to line 106. Change it to `body[\\\"approval\\\"] = {**state.pending_approval, \\\"description\\\": sanitize_reply(state.pending_approval[\\\"description\\\"], CFG[\\\"output\\\"][\\\"allowed_link_hosts\\\"])}`.\",\n  \"Open `src/agent.py` line 188. Use fixed text, or `redact(exc.detail)`, in the returned message.\",\n  \"Create a test with a secret-like value in a tool error and a link in an approval. Check both are cleaned.\"],\n \"Tool errors and approval text sent onward contain no secrets and no unlisted links.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"R04\",[\"tool:search_policies\",\"data:retrieval-db\"],\n \"The handbook cache is keyed by the query only. One employee can read another employee's private HR chunks.\",\n [\"Do B02 first. It changes the cache key in `src/retrieval.py` lines 40 to 46.\",\n  \"Create the test below to prove two employees get separate cache entries, and run it.\"],\n \"Two employees who run the same query never share a cache entry.\",\"small\",\n test=dict(file=\"tests/test_retrieval_key.py\",code=\"from src.retrieval import PolicyIndex\\n\\n\\ndef test_cache_key_differs_per_employee():\\n    idx = PolicyIndex(None, 5, 900.0)\\n    assert idx._key('leave policy', 'e1') != idx._key('leave policy', 'e2')\\n\",run=\"python -m pytest tests/test_retrieval_key.py\"))\nadd(\"R07\",[\"unit:src/agent.py\",\"data:audit-log\"],\n \"Only model-call records store how full the context was. Tool actions and gateway decisions do not.\",\n [\"Open `src/agent.py` and go to lines 193 and 100. Add `context_tokens=` and `context_tokens_method=` to each `self.audit.record` call. Keep the last measured value in `state.extra`.\",\n  \"In `src/gateway_client.py` line 71 add an `X-Context-Tokens` header. In `src/gateway.py` line 137 store it in a new column of `audit.gateway_decisions` in `migrations/001_init.sql`.\",\n  \"Run a test with one tool call and check its audit row has `context_tokens`.\"],\n \"Every tool action row in `audit.events` has a context size in tokens.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"R08\",[\"data:audit-log\",\"agent\"],\n \"No security detection rules or alert routing are in the repository. They may exist elsewhere.\",\n [\"Ask the security team for the detection rules and alert routes for denied calls, stop events, approval failures, quota stops and audit failures.\",\n  \"Ask them to send a test alert. Record the time it reached the security responder.\",\n  \"Save the rules and the test result in the review record.\"],\n \"Saved rules and a timed test alert show the five event types reach a security responder.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"R09\",[\"unit:src/agent.py\",\"agent\"],\n \"Only fixed per-run limits exist. Nothing detects risky chains of allowed actions or changes with context size.\",\n [\"Open `src/budgets.py` and go to line 62. Add a new class `SequenceWatch` that counts repeated denials and a read followed by a send in one run.\",\n  \"Call it in `src/agent.py` after line 120. When it trips, call `self.audit.record(ctx, \\\"sequence_alert\\\", ...)` and stop the run.\",\n  \"Add per-context-size limits to `config/agent.yaml` lines 13 to 18.\",\n  \"Create a test that makes three denied calls in a row. Check that the run stops.\"],\n \"A run with repeated denied calls is stopped and logged as a `sequence_alert`.\",\"large\")\nadd(\"R10\",[\"agent\"],\n \"No second reviewer of the agent's actions exists, and no decision is recorded on whether deliberate misalignment is in scope.\",\n [\"Ask the security lead to decide whether a misaligned agent is in scope. Write the decision in `release/manifest.yaml`.\",\n  \"If it is in scope, add a second check that sees only the proposed action, not untrusted text. Build a set of labeled test runs.\",\n  \"Measure how many bad runs the check misses. Save the result in the review record.\"],\n \"A written scope decision exists, and if in scope, a measured miss rate is on file.\",\"large\")\nadd(\"R11\",[\"tool:escalate_to_human\",\"unit:src/agent.py\"],\n \"The direct route skips the gateway stop check, and no dated stop drill is on file.\",\n DR[:2]+[\"Open `src/agent.py` and go to line 106. Add `await self.stop.raise_if_stopped(ctx)` before `state.budget.check_tool_call()`, so each tool call checks the stop flag.\",\n  \"Run a stop drill in a test cluster. Insert a fleet stop flag and record the time until the run stops.\",\n  \"Save the drill date and time in `docs/drills/` in the ops repo.\"],\n \"A dated drill shows a stop flag halts new tool calls within 10 seconds.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"R12\",[\"unit:src/agent.py\",\"tool:file_leave_request\",\"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n \"There is no rule for each tool on what happens when a run stops. Unknown results are not held for checking.\",\n [\"Open `config/tools.yaml`. Under each tool add `on_stop: abandon` for reads or `on_stop: hold_for_review` for writes.\",\n  \"Open `src/gateway_client.py` line 85. When the result is unknown, raise `ToolError` with a flag `unknown_outcome=True`.\",\n  \"In `src/agent.py` line 183, write a `hold` audit record for that case. Refuse any later call with the same arguments until a person clears it.\",\n  \"Create a test that times out a write call. Check that a hold record exists.\"],\n \"A timed-out write leaves a hold record that blocks the same action until a person clears it.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"R13\",[\"unit:src/agent.py\",\"data:audit-log\"],\n \"Some tool calls leave no linked audit step, and cancelled or failed calls have no linked outcome.\",\n [\"Open `src/agent.py` line 154. Before the gateway call add `self.audit.record(ctx, \\\"state_recheck\\\", ...)` with `parent_step_id=state.last_step`, and one for the result.\",\n  \"Open `src/gateway_client.py` and add a record for the retry. Remove the retry as part of R14 if you can.\",\n  \"In `src/main.py` line 91, add the proposed step ids to the `run_stopped` record so each one has an outcome.\",\n  \"Run one cancelled run and check each `proposed_action` has a linked outcome row.\"],\n \"Every proposed action has a linked outcome row in `audit.events`, including cancelled and failed ones.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"R14\",[\"data:audit-log\",\"mcp:helpdesk\",\"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n \"Approval and audit rows can be changed without notice, and an unclear 503 triggers an automatic resend through the direct route.\",\n DR[:2]+[\"Open `migrations/001_init.sql` line 54. Create a new migration that adds a `row_hash` column to `approvals.grants` and `audit.events`. Hash each row with the previous one.\",\n  \"Verify the chain on resume in `src/approvals.py` line 90, and refuse a record whose hash fails.\",\n  \"Create a test that changes a stored row. Check that resume is refused.\"],\n \"A changed approval row is refused on resume, and an unclear 503 never causes a resend.\",\"large\")\nadd(\"A01\",[\"agent\",\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"],\n \"The agent has its own identity, but the repository does not show that it can be cut off without cutting off the user.\",\n [\"Ask the platform team for the STS policy and database role for `hr-helpdesk-agent`.\",\n  \"Ask them to run a drill that revokes only the agent identity. Check that a user can still sign in to other apps.\",\n  \"Save the drill date and result in the review record.\"],\n \"A dated drill shows the agent identity can be revoked while the user's login still works.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"A02\",[\"unit:src/agent.py\",\"data:audit-log\",\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"],\n \"Refused requests are not logged. Gateway denials for bad logins have 'unknown' in their identity fields.\",\n [\"Open `src/gateway.py` line 132. Fill the unknown fields from the caller's certificate and mark the row `untrusted_caller`.\",\n  \"Open `src/main.py` line 114. Before returning 401, write an audit row with all six fields set to the string `untrusted_caller`.\",\n  \"If that write fails, return 503 instead of 401.\",\n  \"Create a test that sends a bad token. Check an audit row exists.\"],\n \"A request with a bad token creates an audit row in both the agent and the gateway.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"A03\",[\"unit:src/agent.py\",\"agent\"],\n \"The Dockerfile copies files without the hash step covering every input, and the repeat-hash check is not proven.\",\n [\"Open `Dockerfile` line 12. Check that every file copied in is listed in `src/type_id.py` lines 20 and 21.\",\n  \"Create a test that computes the id twice and checks the two values match.\",\n  \"Add a loop to the test that changes one input at a time and checks the id changes each time.\",\n  \"Run the test in `.github/workflows/release.yml` before line 45.\"],\n \"Changing any input file, the model record or the digest changes the agent-type-id.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"A04\",[\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\",\"unit:src/agent.py\"],\n \"The gateway trusts a caller header for the instance, and a resumed run starts a new trace.\",\n [\"Open `src/gateway.py` line 170. Replace the header with a verified value from the token, such as a new `inst` claim set by the STS.\",\n  \"Open `src/main.py` line 147. Store the trace parent with the approval grant and restore it on resume.\",\n  \"Create a test that sends a forged `X-Agent-Instance`. Check that the gateway ignores it.\"],\n \"The gateway uses an instance id from the signed token, and a resumed run continues the original trace.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"A05\",[\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\",\"data:audit-log\"],\n \"The gateway cannot stop one agent type, and its audit rows hold only ids the caller supplied.\",\n [\"Do B04 first. It adds the agent type to the gateway stop query in `src/gateway.py` line 100.\",\n  \"Open `src/gateway.py` line 138. Replace the header values with ids from the verified token.\",\n  \"Create a stop flag for one agent type in a test cluster. Check that the gateway refuses that type only.\"],\n \"A stop flag for one agent type blocks that type at the gateway and no other.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"C01\",[\"agent\"],\n \"The release manifest leaves out issuer and audience settings, and most artifacts have no owner or fixed reference.\",\n [\"Open `release/manifest.yaml`. After line 36 add the SSO issuer and audience from `src/main.py` lines 36 and 37 and the gateway ones from `src/gateway.py` lines 32 and 33.\",\n  \"Add the MCP protocol version, each tool fingerprint from `config/tools.yaml`, and `retrieval.cache_ttl_seconds`.\",\n  \"Give every artifact an `owner` and a `digest` or `commit`. Update the CI step on line 50 of `.github/workflows/release.yml` if it writes new fields.\"],\n \"Every artifact in the release manifest has an owner and an immutable reference.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"C02\",[\"agent\"],\n \"One catch-all team owns the Dockerfile, dependencies and most source files, and no emergency-change path exists.\",\n [\"Open `CODEOWNERS`. After line 1 add `/Dockerfile`, `/requirements.txt` and `/src/` lines owned by `@acme/people-platform @acme/security-engineering`.\",\n  \"Create `docs/emergency-change.md` that says who can approve an urgent change and how it is reviewed afterward.\",\n  \"Check in GitHub that a pull request touching `Dockerfile` asks for the security team.\"],\n \"A pull request that changes `Dockerfile` or `requirements.txt` needs review from the security team.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"C03\",[\"agent\"],\n \"Only the agent checks its own identity at start. No outside process compares the running setup to the approved manifest.\",\n [\"Open `k8s/admission.yaml`. After line 81 add a Kyverno rule that checks the pod's `AGENT_TYPE_ID` and image digest against `release/manifest.yaml`.\",\n  \"Or create a CronJob `k8s/manifest-check.yaml` that compares them every hour and alerts on a mismatch.\",\n  \"Deploy a pod with a wrong id in a test cluster and check it is refused or alerted.\"],\n \"A pod whose id differs from the approved manifest is refused or raises an alert.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"C04\",[\"agent\"],\n \"No check compares running prompts, tools, permissions or network rules with the approved baseline.\",\n [\"Create `k8s/drift-check.yaml`, a CronJob that reads the live pod, config map and network policy and compares them with `release/manifest.yaml`.\",\n  \"Set the alert target and the response time in `config/agent.yaml`, for example `drift: {alert: security-oncall, respond_minutes: 60}`.\",\n  \"Change a network rule in a test cluster. Check that an alert arrives.\"],\n \"A changed prompt, tool list or network rule raises an alert within one hour.\",\"large\")\nadd(\"C05\",[\"model:claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\"],\n \"Nothing re-tests the agent on a schedule or watches for provider notices about the pinned model.\",\n [\"Create `.github/workflows/retest.yml` that runs `python -m pytest tests/release` every week against the pinned model.\",\n  \"Add a step that opens an issue if the provider's deprecation page lists `claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929`.\",\n  \"Run the workflow once and keep the result.\"],\n \"A scheduled job re-runs the release tests weekly and the last run is on file.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"C06\",[\"unit:src/agent.py\",\"agent\"],\n \"The release job runs a test folder that does not exist, and no results are stored with the release.\",\n [\"Open `.github/workflows/release.yml` line 58. Add `test-results.xml` to the upload `path` list.\",\n  \"On line 29 change the command to `python -m pytest -q tests/release --junitxml=test-results.xml`.\",\n  \"Create `tests/release/` with one test of an attack that must be refused and one allowed task that must work.\",\n  \"Push a branch and check the release job uploads the results.\"],\n \"Each release stores test results tied to its manifest, including at least one attack test.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"C07\",[\"agent\",\"model:claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\"],\n \"No approved recovery setup or tested rollback exists, and the model has no recorded retirement date.\",\n [\"Open `release/manifest.yaml`. After line 42 add `retirement_date:` from the provider's deprecation page and a `recovery:` block with the last good digest.\",\n  \"Open `.github/workflows/release.yml`. After line 75 add a `rollback` job that deploys a digest chosen by hand.\",\n  \"Run the rollback job in a test cluster. Keep the run link.\"],\n \"A rollback to the last good digest has been run and the model retirement date is in the manifest.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"C08\",[\"data:audit-log\",\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"],\n \"Traces cannot be tied to a stored release manifest, and audit rows are kept about six weeks, not six months.\",\n [\"Open `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml` line 35. Change `KEEP_PARTITIONS` from `\\\"6\\\"` to `\\\"30\\\"` for about six months of weekly partitions.\",\n  \"Open `src/gateway.py` line 138. Log the agent type id from the verified token.\",\n  \"Store each release manifest by agent type id in a table, in a new migration. Fill it in the release workflow.\",\n  \"Check that a trace's agent type id returns one manifest.\"],\n \"A trace id leads to its release manifest, and audit rows stay for six months.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"E01\",[\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\",\"mcp:hris\",\"mcp:helpdesk\"],\n \"The inventory leaves out the gateway, STS, registry, audit and stop services, and lists only one owner each.\",\n [\"Open `release/manifest.yaml` lines 53 to 55. Add entries for `hr-tool-gateway`, the STS, the image registry, Postgres audit and the stop service.\",\n  \"For each entry add `agent_team_owner` and `platform_owner` or `vendor_owner`.\",\n  \"Ask each platform team to confirm their entry.\"],\n \"Every outside service is listed with an owner on the agent team and one on the platform or vendor side.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"E02\",[\"agent\"],\n \"No scan for known vulnerabilities runs in CI, and no approval records exist for dependencies.\",\n [\"Open `.github/workflows/release.yml`. After line 28 add `- run: pip-audit --require-hashes -r requirements.txt`.\",\n  \"Create `release/dependencies.yaml` with the publisher, permissions and update source of each package in `requirements.txt`.\",\n  \"Add the same for each remote tool server in `config/tools.yaml` line 13.\"],\n \"The release job fails when a dependency has a known vulnerability.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"E03\",[\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\",\"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n \"Tool changes are checked only every 300 seconds, list changes are ignored, and a gateway 503 skips the check.\",\n DR[:2]+[\"Open `src/gateway.py` line 213. Call `refresh_fingerprints()` when a `list_changed` notice arrives, and before each first use after a refresh.\",\n  \"In `refresh_fingerprints`, record the server's version in `config/tools.yaml` under `servers`.\",\n  \"Change one tool description in a test server. Check that the gateway disables the tool.\"],\n \"A changed tool description disables the tool at the gateway, and there is no bypass.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"E04\",[\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\",\"mcp:hris\",\"mcp:helpdesk\"],\n \"Tool metadata is only checked by fingerprint. Nothing scans names, descriptions or schemas for hidden instructions.\",\n [\"Open `src/gateway.py`. After line 63 add a function `scan_metadata(tool)` that rejects control characters, encoded text, and phrases like 'ignore previous'.\",\n  \"Call it for each field in the fingerprint list on line 54. If it fails or raises an error, add the tool to `_disabled`.\",\n  \"Limit each field's length in the same function.\",\n  \"Create a test with a description holding a hidden instruction. Check that the tool is disabled.\"],\n \"A tool whose metadata contains hidden instructions is disabled before the model sees it.\",\"large\")\nadd(\"E05\",[\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"],\n \"Lookalike or duplicate tool names are only logged. They are not blocked, and similar-looking letters are not caught.\",\n [\"Open `src/gateway.py` line 67. Replace `log.error(...)` with `_disabled.add(...)` for both tools and raise a `ValueError`.\",\n  \"On line 65 widen the normalization to map lookalike letters, for example with the `confusable_homoglyphs` package.\",\n  \"Create a test with two servers that list `get_balance` and `get-bаlance` (Cyrillic а). Check both tools are disabled.\"],\n \"Two tools with lookalike names are both disabled until a person reviews them.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"E06\",[\"tool:escalate_to_human\",\"mcp:helpdesk\",\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"],\n \"When the gateway returns 503 or is down, the agent calls the helpdesk server itself. All gateway checks and logs are skipped.\",\n DR+[DRV],\"With the gateway down, `escalate_to_human` fails and no call reaches the helpdesk server.\",\"small\")\nadd(\"E09\",[\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\",\"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n \"A stop does not cancel tokens already issued for 300 seconds, and the direct route skips the stop check.\",\n DR[:2]+[\"Open `src/credentials.py` line 20. Change `TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS` to `10`, the stop time in `config/agent.yaml`, so tokens expire at about the same time.\",\n  \"Keep a list of in-flight calls in `src/gateway_client.py` and write it to the audit log when a stop is seen.\",\n  \"Run a stop drill and check that calls fail after 10 seconds.\"],\n \"After a stop, no call succeeds for longer than 10 seconds.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"E10\",[\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\",\"data:audit-log\"],\n \"Gateway audit rows lack verified identity and trace fields, vendor receipt ids, and are written after the action.\",\n [\"Open `src/gateway.py` line 190. Move the `allow` audit write before the upstream call on line 180, and record a result row afterward.\",\n  \"On lines 137 to 139 use values from the verified token, and save the vendor's request id in a new `vendor_receipt` column in `migrations/001_init.sql`.\",\n  \"Remove the direct route as in B01.\",\n  \"Run one call and check both rows exist.\"],\n \"A gateway audit row exists before each upstream call and holds verified identity fields.\",\"medium\")\nadd(\"E11\",[\"data:audit-log\"],\n \"Audit rows are kept about six weeks, not six months, and no check finds changed or missing rows.\",\n [\"Open `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml` line 35. Change `KEEP_PARTITIONS` from `\\\"6\\\"` to `\\\"30\\\"`.\",\n  \"In a new migration add a sequence number and a hash chain column to `audit.events` and `audit.gateway_decisions`.\",\n  \"Create a daily job that alerts on a gap or a bad hash.\",\n  \"Move the gateway write in `src/gateway.py` line 190 ahead of the upstream call.\"],\n \"Audit rows stay for six months and a missing row raises an alert.\",\"large\")\nadd(\"E12\",[\"agent\",\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"],\n \"No incident runbook, fleet impact query or outside-reporting owner is in the repository.\",\n [\"Ask the security team for the runbook for a bad tool server or vendor.\",\n  \"Run the drill. Keep the impact query, quarantine and revocation records, alert times and the name of the person who decides on outside reporting.\",\n  \"Note that the gateway stop query in `src/gateway.py` line 99 ignores the agent type.\"],\n \"A drill record shows the impact query, a quarantine and a named reporting decision-maker.\",\"medium\")\n\nn=0\nfor f in d['findings']:\n    if f['rating'] in ('gap','needs_evidence'):\n        t=T.pop(f['item'])\n        f['components']=t['components']; f['fix']=t['fix']; f['assignee']=None\n        n+=1\nprint(n,'left',list(T))\njson.dump(d,open(F,'w'),indent=2)\nPYEOF"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01YPeAcnkXeYU4Tdrrckx9pc":{"cwd":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-action-2oj403r7/agent"}}}
